+        // SovereignOS: a locked device must not advertise that it has more than one user, on any
+        // surface, including the real owner's own. A coercer holding the locked device is an
+        // earlier and more common point in the duress scenario than one holding a decoy session:
+        // if the lock screen shows two profiles, the mechanism is defeated before it is invoked.
+        // Gated on a decoy actually existing so a device without one is bit-for-bit stock, and
+        // the owner keeps lock-screen switching if they ever create an ordinary second user.
+        // Display-only: user creation and user switching do not consult this method.
+        if (hasDecoyUser() && isDeviceCurrentlyLocked()) {
+            return false;
+        }
+
